<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: CZECH JANUARY JOBLESS JUMPS TO 4.0 PCT (3.5 DEC).</title>
<headline>CZECH JANUARY JOBLESS JUMPS TO 4.0 PCT (3.5 DEC).</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of jobless in the Czech Republic at the end of January stood at 205,185, or 4.0 percent of the workforce, up from 3.5 percent in December, the Czech Labour and Social Affairs ministry said on Monday.</p>
<p>The ministry has said that a change in methodology from the beginning of 1997 to comply with OECD guidelines, could influence the unemployment rate by up to plus/minus 0.1 percent of the total rate.  </p>
<p> CZECH UNEMPLOYMENT	    JAN 1997    DEC 1996     JAN 1996</p>
<p>  number of jobless	    205,185     186,339	 164,430</p>
<p>  pct of workforce		 4.0	   3.5	     3.1</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
